  "conclusion": "A per-request TLS certificate exception reaches the public portal, web map and OLD_DATA Dushanbe parcel-layer metadata. Actual count, spatial and object-ID reads return ArcGIS error 400 through both FeatureServer and MapServer, including on a second network. CADASTR_NEW parcel-layer metadata times out after 55 seconds locally and 80 seconds on the second network despite a completed TLS handshake. No nonempty parcel response was obtained; the evidence points to a provider-side data-service failure whose exact internal cause is unexposed. The certificate exception is working.",
  "nextStep": "Retry the published OLD_DATA/OLD_DATA/FeatureServer/6 and MapServer/6 queries, plus CADASTR/CADASTR_NEW/FeatureServer/1, after the service recovers. A source-specific certificate exception is authorized; normal certificate validation remains the default. After obtaining polygons, audit local coverage, validity/overlaps, cadastral-code availability and repeatability before enabling the source.",
